notes toilet_type: Meaning (cont.): the facility is unimproved OR improved but SHARED with other households, so a plain own-toilet yes/no cannot decide the indicator: it misses an unshared but unimproved pit latrine, and it misses a flush toilet shared between four
notes toilet_type: Meaning (cont.): families.
notes toilet_type: Question: What kind of toilet does your household use at your usual home?
notes toilet_type: Source: NITI Aayog National MPI sanitation indicator (improved/unimproved and shared/not)
notes drinking_water: Module F - Housing, amenities and assets; origin: asked
notes drinking_water: Meaning: Self-reported, not enumerator-observed: by design the interview happens away from the respondent's usual home (Kedarnath route sites, not their native place), so the enumerator cannot see it. Codes 1-6 are improved sources, 7-9
notes drinking_water: Meaning (cont.): unimproved, following the JMP/NFHS taxonomy NITI Aayog's MPI indicator rests on.
notes drinking_water: Question: What is your main source of drinking water at your usual home?
notes drinking_water: Source: NITI Aayog National MPI drinking-water indicator (JMP improved/unimproved taxonomy)
notes water_on_premises: Module F - Housing, amenities and assets; origin: asked
notes water_on_premises: Meaning: On-premises vs. fetched. NITI counts even an IMPROVED source as deprived when it is more than a 30-minute round trip away, so source alone cannot decide the indicator -- this and the next item supply the missing limb.
