notes shock_loss_amount: Module I - Food security, shocks and coping; origin: asked
notes shock_loss_amount: Meaning: Shock MAGNITUDE. Incidence alone cannot support a vulnerability-as-uninsured-exposure-to-risk analysis: VER asks how far consumption moves per unit of shock, and without a size there is no per unit. A rough figure is expected --
notes shock_loss_amount: Meaning (cont.): the quantity of interest is the order of magnitude against household consumption, not the rupee.
notes shock_loss_amount: Question: Because of that, about how much did your household lose in earnings, or have to spend? (Rs)
notes shock_loss_amount: Skip rule: Ask only if distress_event_last365d is not empty
notes shock_loss_amount: Source: Ligon and Schechter 2003; Dercon and Krishnan 2000 (VER needs shock magnitude, not only incidence)
notes shock_month: Module I - Food security, shocks and coping; origin: asked
notes shock_month: Meaning: Shock TIMING, which is what matches the event to the monthly income calendar in Module C and to the season the household was in. A shock during the Yatra season and the same shock during the closure are different events for a
notes shock_month: Meaning (cont.): household earning its whole year in six months.
notes shock_month: Question: In which month did that happen?
notes shock_month: Skip rule: Ask only if distress_event_last365d is not empty
notes shock_month: Source: Dercon and Krishnan 2000 (seasonal timing of shocks); project design
notes shock_coping: Module I - Food security, shocks and coping; origin: asked
notes shock_coping: Meaning: Check-all. The single-answer version forced a choice between 'sold or pawned assets' and 'cut consumption' -- which are precisely the two responses asset-smoothing theory (Carter and Zimmerman) says to compare, since a household
notes shock_coping: Meaning (cont.): facing a survival constraint may cut consumption specifically to defend its assets. Made mutually exclusive, the test was impossible.
notes shock_coping: Question: How did your household manage? Check every one they used.
notes shock_coping: Skip rule: Ask only if any shock was reported
notes shock_coping: Source: Coping strategies in VEP studies; Carter and Zimmerman 2000 on asset versus consumption smoothing
