notes total_cons_pm: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
notes total_cons_pm: Meaning: Food (annual-average month above) + fuel + toiletries + transport/communication + rent (each annual-average) + the four monthly-equivalent annual items. This is a true annual-average monthly figure, not a single-season snapshot.
notes total_cons_pm: Formula: food_pm (now incl. packaged) + pan_tobacco_pm + fuel_pm + routine_misc_pm + transport_comm_pm + rent_pm + clothing_pm + education_pm + medical_pm + durables_pm
notes total_cons_pm: Source: Chaudhuri et al. 2002 welfare measure; season-weighting added for a migrant population
notes cons_pc_pm: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
notes cons_pc_pm: Meaning: Household consumption per month divided by household size, rounded. This is the VEP outcome (its log).
notes cons_pc_pm: Formula: round(total_cons_pm / hhsize)
notes cons_pc_pm: Source: Chaudhuri et al. 2002
notes cons_pc_pm_narrow: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
notes cons_pc_pm_narrow: Meaning: Only the non-lumpy items (food incl. packaged, pan/tobacco, fuel, toiletries, transport/communication, rent), each already an annual-average month, per person. Leaves out the annual items, as in Dercon and Krishnan 2000. For
notes cons_pc_pm_narrow: Meaning (cont.): robustness of the variance model; not comparable with the poverty line.
notes cons_pc_pm_narrow: Formula: (food_pm + pan_tobacco_pm + fuel_pm + routine_misc_pm + transport_comm_pm + rent_pm) / hhsize
notes cons_pc_pm_narrow: Source: Dercon and Krishnan 2000 (narrow non-food to avoid seasonal lumps)
notes cons_pc_ae_pm: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
notes cons_pc_ae_pm: Meaning: Household consumption divided by (adults + 0.5 x children under 15), where adults = household size minus children under 15. One simple scale; the choice of scale is a sensitivity check.
notes cons_pc_ae_pm: Formula: total_cons_pm / (hhsize - n_children_u15 + 0.5*n_children_u15)
notes cons_pc_ae_pm: Source: Adult-equivalent practice (Awuni et al. 2023; Claro et al. 2010 on per-capita versus adult-equivalent)
notes poverty_line: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
notes poverty_line: Meaning: Sethu, Surya and Ruthu (2024) construct TWO lines for 2022-23 by the Rangarajan method: Rs 2,515 per capita per month rural and Rs 3,639 urban. Which applies is decided by home_rural_urban -- the respondent's USUAL place of
notes poverty_line: Meaning (cont.): residence, not the Yatra worksite. Until this variable existed the build applied the rural line to everyone, which measured urban-resident workers against a line 31 percent too low and understated their poverty.
notes poverty_line: Formula: 2515 if home_rural_urban==1, else 3639
notes poverty_line: Source: Sethu, Surya and Ruthu 2024 (Rangarajan method on HCES 2022-23), both lines
notes poor: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
notes poor: Meaning: 1 if per-capita monthly consumption is below the rural or urban line that applies to this respondent.
notes poor: Formula: cons_pc_pm < poverty_line
notes poor: Source: Sethu, Surya and Ruthu 2024
notes poor_sensitivity_cpi: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
notes poor_sensitivity_cpi: Meaning: 1 if below the Rangarajan and Dev 2024 CPI-adjusted line; robustness only.
notes poor_sensitivity_cpi: Formula: cons_pc_pm < 1850
notes poor_sensitivity_cpi: Source: Rangarajan and Dev 2024
notes durables_count: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
notes durables_count: Meaning: Legacy six-item count kept only so earlier outputs stay reproducible. DO NOT use for the MPI: the asset indicator is mpi_asset_deprived, which applies NITI's actual rule to its actual eight-item list.
notes durables_count: Formula: owns_tv + owns_radio + owns_bicycle + owns_motorcycle + owns_car + owns_fridge
notes durables_count: Source: Constructed
notes productive_assets_count: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
notes productive_assets_count: Meaning: Sum of the six productive-asset binaries (livestock, pony/mule, shop/stall, work vehicle, work equipment).
notes productive_assets_count: Formula: owns_cow_buffalo + owns_goat_sheep + owns_pony_mule + owns_shop_stall + owns_work_vehicle + owns_work_equipment
notes productive_assets_count: Source: Constructed
notes water_deprived: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
notes water_deprived: Meaning: NITI rule, BOTH limbs: deprived if the source is unimproved (codes 7-9), OR the source is improved but the round trip to fetch it takes over 30 minutes. The second limb could not be evaluated at all before water_on_premises and
notes water_deprived: Meaning (cont.): water_fetch_minutes existed.
notes water_deprived: Formula: inrange(drinking_water,7,9) | (water_on_premises==0 & water_fetch_minutes>30)
notes water_deprived: Source: NITI Aayog National MPI drinking-water indicator
notes cooking_fuel_deprived: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
notes cooking_fuel_deprived: Meaning: NITI rule: deprived if the household cooks with firewood, dung, crop residue/shrubs, charcoal or coal (codes 6-10). Kerosene (5) is NOT counted, because NITI's own list does not name it; the global MPI does count it, so this is a
notes cooking_fuel_deprived: Meaning (cont.): documented departure and the raw fuel code is retained so either rule can be applied later.
notes cooking_fuel_deprived: Formula: inlist(cooking_fuel,6,7,8,9,10)
notes cooking_fuel_deprived: Source: NITI Aayog National MPI cooking-fuel indicator
notes mpi_asset_count: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
notes mpi_asset_count: Meaning: Radio, TV, telephone, computer, animal cart, bicycle, motorbike, refrigerator -- NITI's own list. Car or truck is NOT in this count; it is a separate limb of the indicator.
notes mpi_asset_count: Formula: owns_radio + owns_tv + owns_phone + owns_computer + owns_animal_cart + owns_bicycle + owns_motorcycle + owns_fridge
notes mpi_asset_count: Source: NITI Aayog National MPI assets indicator
notes mpi_asset_deprived: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
notes mpi_asset_deprived: Meaning: NITI rule exactly: deprived if the household does not own MORE THAN ONE of the eight small assets AND does not own a car or truck. The previous version summed six assets into a plain count, which is not NITI's rule and is not
notes mpi_asset_deprived: Meaning (cont.): comparable to any published National MPI figure.
notes mpi_asset_deprived: Formula: mpi_asset_count <= 1 & owns_car == 0
notes mpi_asset_deprived: Source: NITI Aayog National MPI assets indicator
notes child_school_dep: Module X - Constructed variables (built in Stata from the asked variables); origin: constructed
